# Only the steward-owned paths are code-owned.
# listings/ and packs/ are deliberately not, so the checks alone gate them and a
# validated listing can merge itself without a human (RFC 0033).
#
# CODEOWNERS itself lives under .github/, so the second line covers it.
#
# The checks are code-owned wherever they live. A pull request runs the workflow
# and the tools as they exist on its own merge ref, so a listing that could also
# edit the schema or the checker would be arriving with its own gate.

/index-status.toml @KSAModding/content-manager-stewards
/.github/          @KSAModding/content-manager-stewards
/tools/            @KSAModding/content-manager-stewards
/schemas/          @KSAModding/content-manager-stewards
